# Content Layer — Events and Geological Periods

[`Content.svelte`](src/lib/components/main/content/Content.svelte) renders the foreground timeline content. Viewport pan/zoom and screen→layout coordinate mapping belong in [`Main.svelte`](src/lib/components/main/Main.svelte) — see [`main-svelte.mdc`](main-svelte.mdc).

## Layout

- **Geological periods zone** — top flex item in the content area (above the label band), basis `GEOLOGICAL_PERIODS_ZONE_HEIGHT_RATIO` (50%) from [`layout.ts`](src/lib/constants/layout.ts). Rendered only when `$displaySettings.showGeologicalPeriods` is on. Renders `GeologicalPeriodCard` items from layouts built by [`geologicalPeriodLayout.ts`](src/lib/utils/geologicalPeriodLayout.ts).
- **Events zone** — flex item that fills the remaining content area above the label band (the full area when geological periods are hidden). Renders [`EventCard`](src/lib/components/main/content/events/EventCard.svelte) items from layouts built by [`eventLayout.ts`](src/lib/utils/eventLayout.ts). Lane stacking follows the measured zone height.
- **Visibility** — `$displaySettings.showGeologicalPeriods` from [`displayStore.ts`](src/lib/stores/displayStore.ts) shows or hides the geological periods zone. The loading state uses the locale-aware `messages` map in `Content.svelte`.
- Data loads on mount via [`fetchEvents()`](src/lib/api.ts) and [`fetchGeologicalPeriods()`](src/lib/api.ts) from [`api.ts`](src/lib/api.ts).

## Shared span positioning

Horizontal span math lives in [`spanPosition.ts`](src/lib/utils/spanPosition.ts):

- `yearToLayoutX()` — maps a year to layout-space X (same axis as timeline ticks)
- `getClampedSpanPosition()` — clamped `{ x, width, centerX, startX, endX }` for viewport-visible spans
- `snapLayoutX()` — rounds X for crisp 1px markers

Used by geological periods, event layout, and timeline ticks.

Edge-blur span backgrounds use [`spanBandStyle.ts`](src/lib/utils/spanBandStyle.ts) + [`SpanBand.svelte`](src/lib/components/main/content/SpanBand.svelte).

## Event positioning

All event geometry is computed in [`eventLayout.ts`](src/lib/utils/eventLayout.ts) via `buildEventLayouts()` and passed to [`EventCard.svelte`](src/lib/components/main/content/events/EventCard.svelte) as an `EventLayout` object. Components do not compute their own X/Y. Every event is an [`EventConnectorCard.svelte`](src/lib/components/main/content/events/EventConnectorCard.svelte): a fixed-size card plus the same Bézier funnel. Detail uses [`DetailPanel.svelte`](src/lib/components/main/content/DetailPanel.svelte) inline when it fits the card, otherwise [`DetailPopover.svelte`](src/lib/components/main/content/DetailPopover.svelte).

Date ranges come from [`eventSpan.ts`](src/lib/utils/eventSpan.ts): `date ± dateUncertainty/2` when uncertainty exists; otherwise a point at `date`.

### Display tiers (zoom-dependent)

| Tier | Condition | Shape |
|------|-----------|--------|
| `point` | No uncertainty, or span `< 1px` | Fixed-width card and a Bézier funnel down to a point at `date` |
| `range`, span `≤` card width | `1px ≤ span ≤ EVENT_CARD_WIDTH` | Same card and funnel, bottom is the uncertainty span |
| `range`, span wider than the card | span `> EVENT_CARD_WIDTH` | No funnel. The text block widens to the visible span, and the rectangle runs from the events-zone floor up to the top of that text |

**Connector cards (`EventConnectorCard`)** — one component for every event. A point or a span no wider than the card keeps the rounded card plus a Bézier funnel. The funnel always has at least `EVENT_CONNECTOR_MIN_HEIGHT_PX` of height, including lane 0, and raised lanes add `lane * laneStep`. A wider span drops the funnel: the text block uses the span's x and width, and the same rectangle continues straight down to `EVENT_CARD_MIN_BOTTOM_OFFSET_PX`. Its `markerHeight` is only the lane lift (`lane * laneStep`), so lane 0 is just the text block on the floor. The shape's CSS `bottom` is `layout.bottom - layout.markerHeight`. `markerHeight` is the funnel only. Text is an HTML overlay. Path geometry is built by [`eventDateMarkerPath.ts`](src/lib/utils/eventDateMarkerPath.ts). Card height is measured at runtime via `ResizeObserver`. Uses `data-event-connector` alongside `data-event-card`. Fit checks for inline detail live in [`detailContentFit.ts`](src/lib/utils/detailContentFit.ts).

Fixed-width cards are centered on the best-estimate date with viewport edge clamping (`getEventCardXPosition()`).

### Vertical lane stacking

- Overlap detection uses rendered horizontal footprint: `min(anchor.x, card.x)` to `max(anchor.x + anchor.width, card.x + card.width)`
- Greedy lane assignment sorted by collision left edge
- Default lane step: `EVENT_CARD_HEIGHT + EVENT_LANE_PEEK_GAP_PX` (25px peek), above `EVENT_CONNECTOR_MIN_HEIGHT_PX`
- Uniform compression when the stack exceeds `eventsZoneHeight`

### Visibility filter

Events are visible when their date range overlaps the viewport (`isEventRangeVisible()`), not when `event.date` alone is in range.

## Geological Period Positioning

- Horizontal span positioning uses `getClampedSpanPosition()` from [`spanPosition.ts`](src/lib/utils/spanPosition.ts); [`geologicalPeriodLayout.ts`](src/lib/utils/geologicalPeriodLayout.ts) exposes `getGeologicalPeriodHorizontalPosition()` as a thin wrapper.
- Vertical geometry (height, bottom offset, z-index by depth) comes from `getGeologicalPeriodCardGeometry()` in [`geologicalPeriodLayout.ts`](src/lib/utils/geologicalPeriodLayout.ts). Child periods occupy `GEOLOGICAL_PERIOD_CHILD_HEIGHT_RATIO` (50%) of the parent height.
- Card backgrounds use per-period `color` resolved at load time with neighbor blending via `getSpanBandBackgroundStyle()` in [`spanBandStyle.ts`](src/lib/utils/spanBandStyle.ts). Text uses `var(--theme-on-media)`.
- **Color resolution** — [`geologicalPeriodColors.ts`](src/lib/utils/geologicalPeriodColors.ts) via `resolveGeologicalPeriodColors()` in [`fetchGeologicalPeriods()`](src/lib/api.ts):
  - Eons (`parentPeriodId === null`) use the explicit `color` from [`geologicalPeriods.jsonc`](static/geologicalPeriods.jsonc).
  - Child periods without `color` receive LCH variations derived from their resolved parent (chroma.js).
  - Optional `color` on any period overrides derivation and becomes the base for its own children.
- When selected, a period shows [`DetailPopover.svelte`](src/lib/components/main/content/DetailPopover.svelte) (`data-geological-period-popover`, z-index `1100`) when inline detail does not fit; layout from `getGeologicalPeriodPopoverLayout()` in [`geologicalPeriodLayout.ts`](src/lib/utils/geologicalPeriodLayout.ts) using shared [`detailPopoverLayout.ts`](src/lib/utils/detailPopoverLayout.ts).

## Click-to-Front

- Selection state in `Content.svelte`:
  - `topCardType`: `"event" | "geologicalPeriod" | null`
  - `topCardEventId` / `topCardGeologicalPeriodId` — stable ids, not visible index
  - `hoveredCardEventId` + `onCardHover` — events only; raises cards temporarily while the pointer is over them
- Z-index tiers on every event connector:
  - Selected: `1000`
  - Hovered (not selected): `999`
  - Default: `980 + lane` (capped at `998`)
- All events render in a single stacking context; lane order applies uniformly across tiers.
- Geological period cards use depth-based z-index from `getGeologicalPeriodCardGeometry()` (base `100`, selected `1000`).
- Clicking a card sets selection on `pointerup` via `bindPointerClick` from [`pointerClickOrDrag.ts`](src/lib/utils/pointerClickOrDrag.ts): selection fires only if pointer movement stays below `POINTER_DRAG_THRESHOLD_PX` (5px), otherwise the event bubbles to `Main.svelte` for pan. Do not use `stopPropagation` on card `pointerdown`.
- Deselect via `Main.svelte` `stopDragging`: on a tap (movement ≤ `POINTER_DRAG_THRESHOLD_PX`) outside `[data-event-card]`, `[data-geological-period-card]`, and `[data-geological-period-popover]`, call `Content.deselectCards()`. Use the pointerdown target (not pointerup target) because pointer capture retargets events. Do not use per-card `clickOutside` — it races with selection.
- Selecting one card type clears the other (`topCardType` enforces mutual exclusivity).

## Styling

- Event visuals use per-event `color` from [`eventColors.ts`](src/lib/utils/eventColors.ts): connector SVG fills/gradients (`EventConnectorCard`) and selection borders via `getEventConnectorStroke()` / `getEventPanelBorderStyle()`. Detached detail uses the shared surface popover (`DetailPopover`). Text on colored surfaces uses `text-on-media`.
- `data-event-card` is a semantic hook for click-outside deselection only — no global CSS in [`app.css`](src/app.css).
- Geological period cards use data-driven `color` with CSS gradients; selection adds `border-selection-outline` and scale transform via `getGeologicalPeriodSelectionTransform()`.
- Localize text with `$currentLocale`: event names, descriptions, and dates via `formatDate(event.date, $currentLocale)`; geological period names via `layout.name[$currentLocale]`.

## Performance

- Filter visible events with range overlap via `isEventRangeVisible()` and `$derived` on viewport boundaries.
- Build event layouts with `$derived` via `buildEventLayouts()`.
- Build visible geological period layouts with `$derived` via `buildVisibleGeologicalPeriodLayouts()`.
- Prefer Svelte 5 runes (`$derived`, `$state`, `$props`, `$effect`) over legacy reactive statements.

